Interoperability and third-party rights
---------------------------------------

Alien is an independent, from-scratch interoperability implementation of the
ACPI/WMI interface that Acer's firmware exposes on Predator systems. It is not
produced by, endorsed by, or affiliated with Acer Inc. "Acer", "Predator", and
"PredatorSense" are trademarks of their respective owners, used here only to
describe the hardware this software works with.

The interface was characterised by observing the firmware directly — reading
ACPI tables, issuing calls, and measuring what the hardware did — and by
studying the vendor's own software for the sole purpose of interoperability.
Every constant in this repository is a fact about a hardware interface.

This repository contains no code, artwork, icons, or other assets taken from
Acer's software. The user interface was written from scratch and does not
imitate the vendor's: it has its own palette and its own layout. Gauges and
status marks are drawn from primitives at run time. The Alien project mark is
original artwork created from scratch by HARTLE.TECH specifically for Alien.
Its creative inspiration comes only from source-film material made available
under Creative Commons; no stock imagery or watermarked material was used.
HARTLE.TECH, as its author, expressly authorizes publication and distribution
of the native SVG and matching raster under GPL-2.0-or-later with the other
project artwork. Neither asset came from Acer or PredatorSense. Extracted
vendor packages, firmware images, and decompiler output are excluded from the
public snapshot and are never distributed with Alien.


Bundled fonts
-------------

The desktop client embeds four unmodified upstream static TrueType font files
so that a single binary renders identically on any distribution. They are
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; the exact upstream notices and
license texts are shipped separately:

  * Archivo — Copyright 2020 The Archivo Project Authors
    https://github.com/Omnibus-Type/Archivo
    code/alien-gui/assets/fonts/Archivo-OFL.txt
  * IBM Plex Mono — Copyright 2017 IBM Corp.
    https://github.com/IBM/plex
    code/alien-gui/assets/fonts/IBMPlex-OFL.txt

"Plex" is IBM's Reserved Font Name. Alien uses that name lawfully because it
ships IBM's unmodified upstream font files. No bundled font is subset, renamed,
or relicensed. Exact pinned revisions and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in
code/alien-gui/assets/fonts/README.md.


Credit
------

The reverse-engineering work behind the Linux Acer gaming WMI ecosystem is
collective. Alien's understanding of the protocol builds on:

  * facer — https://github.com/JafarAkhondali/acer-predator-turbo-and-rgb-keyboard-linux-module
  * Linuwu-Sense — https://github.com/0x7375646F/Linuwu-Sense
  * the in-tree acer-wmi driver in the Linux kernel

Where their published function numbers and payload layouts matched what we
measured, we say so; where our own measurements disagreed or went further, the
source comments record which is which and how it was tested.
